<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">UBS</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1998">1998</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as UBS Group</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">UBS is a Swiss bank formed in 1998 by the merger of the Union Bank of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> and the Swiss Bank Corporation, and one of the world's largest wealth managers. During the financial crisis of 2008 it needed a federal rescue, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> investigation of its role in tax evasion helped end Swiss bank secrecy towards foreign tax authorities. In 2023 it took over its rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/credit-suisse">Credit Suisse</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ubs.jpg" alt="UBS" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JaierRT · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UBS_HQ_Zurich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
